#: Game/Doc.lean:99
msgid "§0 is the **VC-generating walker** — the whole manual\n"
"pipeline, mechanized. From a §1 goal it bridges to the function\n"
"body and walks it statement by statement: straight-line segments are\n"
"discharged by captured symbolic execution, an §2 forks the walk per branch,\n"
"and each §3 is opened by the loop rule. Everything the interpreter can\n"
"answer is answered on the spot; what it cannot invent is *appended* as goals —\n"
"pure mathematics over named atoms, tagged by their role: §4 (the invariant\n"
"holds on entry), §5 (one loop body keeps it), §6 (the measure\n"
"drops), §7/§8 (from the exit facts to the returned value).\n"
"\n"
"Loops need the two pieces of content no tactic can invent — the **invariant**\n"
"and the **decreasing measure**. Hand them over as clauses:\n"
"\n"
"§9\n"
"\n"
"The i-th §10/§11 pair belongs to the i-th §12 (source order; label\n"
"them §13, §14, … when there are several). Binder names must be the\n"
"Python names of the variables **assigned in that loop's body**; everything\n"
"else stays pinned and can be mentioned directly. *Omit* the clauses and the\n"
"walker leaves them as delayed goals §15/§16 — the proof pauses until you\n"
"invent the invariant. An §17 clause states a loop's exit fact\n"
"explicitly — required when a §18 escapes a loop and the code after it\n"
"needs more than the bare invariant."
msgstr ""

